This week we got to meet with a bunch of cool people and had a bunch of lit
meals with members, but one thing that stood out was the foreigners we
interacted with this week lol.

A few reasons why

Met a guy from Ghana and exchanged phone numbers with him in a used
clothing shop on Pday

We were able to contact like 2-3 referrals, one of them is interested in
learning free Japanese with us and in Church

A guy that basically said the church is a lie and we're being brainwashed
came to church with us on Sunday

Our friend Celia (new weekly church attendee) from Brazil calls me her ange=
l

Needless to say, the foreigners have been on fire this past week.

As far as Shinpei's baptism goes, it might be postponed as long as he
doesn't respond to us =F0=9F=98=A2 he's in cahoots with a member so that's =
good. Just
hope he can tell we still care about him!!

One fun thing from this week was getting lunch with 2 25 year Olds, they
bought the meal, it was some tasty sushi. We were able to talk a lot about
the church, invited them, and even gave them some trivia on the last
supper. It was cool. Branch president assigned me to give a talk my last
Sunday here instead of his wife, so hopefully they will be able to come and
hear it.

We also while housing met a friend of one of our friends, and we're gonna
get lunch with them both this week! =F0=9F=98=82

It's been a good week. But it's never easy to keep pressing forward.
Fortunately, it's possible if we rely on the Savior and on the means God
has provided us.

I love you guys. God loves you and knows your trials and burdens. Turn to
Him!

=F0=9F=98=81

Our sweaty backs after biking today

